{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"492423553055931673f361b6fb74533c2b6010547bab018285d416851d581bb9","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira DataCenter adapter pagination guard","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py","test_no_search_issues_call_relies_on_the_default_page_size","_TRANSPORT_SRC","adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py","_search_issues_calls_taking_the_default","commit 4213081d23","adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","search_issues","maxResults"],"problem_keywords":["structural guard","vacuous test","AST scan","module split","pagination","search_issues"],"propositions":["Commit 465d's module split relocated search_issues call sites from transport.py to _base.py and _issues.py without updating the guard's hardcoded scan path, causing the AST predicate to find zero call sites.","The structural guard test_no_search_issues_call_relies_on_the_default_page_size passes unconditionally because it scans transport.py which no longer contains the construct it polices, rendering it unable to detect unpaginated callers added elsewhere in the adapter.","The guard lacks a non-vacuity assertion; if a future module move empties the directory again, the test remains silent rather than failing RED.","The fix must widen the scan from transport.py to all *.py modules in adapters/jira_datacenter/ and add an anti-rot assertion that the predicate observes a non-zero population of search_issues calls."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787795922840530001,"uuid":"444d3336-4be3-456e-8f26-14a8dd8f148f"}